# Dockerfile does `COPY . src/coco-robot-ros2/`, so without this the local
# colcon build tree and any RL checkpoints get baked into the image and
# then built over. Mirrors .gitignore.
#
# Docker anchors every pattern at the context root unless it starts with
# `**/` (Go filepath.Match; see test_docker_context.py). The bare forms
# below therefore only ever matched at the root; the `**/` forms are what
# keep a developer tree's coco_rl/coco_rl/__pycache__ and friends out.
# scripts/container/build.sh sidesteps the question entirely by building
# from `git archive`, which carries none of it.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
build/
install/
log/
.git/
.vscode/
*.swp
**/*.swp
*.egg-info/
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Worktrees. `.claude/worktrees/` holds full checkouts of other branches;
# copying them in would multiply the build context by however many are
# open, and then colcon would try to build every one of them.
.claude/
.codex/

# Measurement data. docs/data/ carries the C2-NAV run evidence -- 8 600
# lines of JSON and per-run logs across c2nav48_live and c2nav49_live. It
# is provenance for the numbers in CLAUDE.md, not something the image
# needs, and it is the largest thing in the repo by file count.
docs/data/

# RL training artifacts, which land at the repo root. Written anchored
# because the intent is "root only": the shipped policy at
# coco_rl/policies/phase5_24deg_s0p0.zip MUST stay in the image, since
# ramp_driver refuses /ramp/climb without it.
#
# A bare `*.zip` would ALSO have been correct -- Docker uses Go's
# filepath.Match, where `*` does not cross `/`, so it never reached the
# nested policy. The leading slash only makes that explicit to the next
# reader, who may (as one did) assume shell-glob semantics and "fix" a
# bug that was not there. coco_rl/test/test_docker_context.py pins both.
/*.zip
*.monitor.csv
